    "executing_assertion": "crates/antecedent-estimate/src/heterogeneity_robust_did/tests.rs::sun_abraham_on_an_unbalanced_panel_matches_the_full_dummy_regression_reference",
    "historical_exposure": "Historical author exposure is unrecorded and remains unknown.",
    "reference_review": {
      "scope": "One simulated unbalanced staggered-adoption panel (cohorts 0, 3, 5 of 40 units, periods 1 to 6, cohort-dependent attrition, no comparison unit at period 6) with known cohort-by-event-time effects: the saturated cohort-by-period coefficients, the pre-adoption leads by event time, the cohort-size-weighted simple average, the unit counts and the dropped-row counts.",
      "independence_basis": "The generator builds one dummy per unit, per period and per cohort-period cell, checks full column rank, and solves with numpy.linalg.lstsq; it then aggregates with cohort sizes. It uses no within transformation, no support screening beyond dropping rows at periods without a never-treated unit, and no production solver, and imports no Antecedent code. The product's Sun-Abraham path is a different computation (within transformation and its own support screening). The executing assertion reads the stored rows into the product, and compares each post-adoption cell estimate and unit counts, each lead, and the simple average at absolute 1e-8, the dropped-row count exactly, and the simple average against the declared truth within 0.1.",
      "historical_exposure": "The reference was written by the repository author alongside the product; independence rests on the different computation described above, not on a separate author. The production estimator source was not consulted for this review.",
      "redistribution": "Repository-authored MIT OR Apache-2.0 generator and deterministic inputs. NumPy is used from an isolated locked script environment outside the product and ordinary CI; no upstream source is stored.",
      "limitations": "One panel and one seed; point estimates only, no standard errors or intervals (the product's bootstrap is not frozen here); never-treated comparison only; no covariates; treatment effects constant within a cohort-period cell. The pre-adoption cells inside cells[] are not individually asserted (the leads are). The sibling fixest comparison is a separate fixture. No calibration.",
